# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for LRPS2 sweeps.
#
# Usage:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=tests/tsan.supp" <harness>
#
# Two categories only.  Anything TSan reports that is not matched here
# is NEW and must be triaged, not added blindly.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACCEPTED BY DESIGN - do not "fix" without an architecture decision.
#
# The EE thread writes GS privileged registers (SMODE1/SMODE2, PMODE,
# DISPFB, ...) directly into shared PS2MEM_GS via gsWrite64_page_00 /
# gsWrite64_generic; the GS side reads them at vsync (GSRenderer::Merge,
# GSState::GetVideoMode / isReallyInterlaced, MTGS::MainLoop's vsync
# path).  Inherited from upstream PCSX2, where priv-reg traffic is
# deliberately not ring-serialized.  Accesses are aligned and
# word-sized on the only supported host (x86-64: single mov, no
# tearing); worst case is a one-frame-stale video mode, which matches
# real-hardware semantics - a mode change mid-scanout is "torn" on a
# real PS2 too.  Serializing these through the MTGS ring would be
# invasive, perf-relevant, and upstream-divergent.
race:GSState::GetVideoMode
race:GSState::isReallyInterlaced
race:gsWrite64_generic
race:gsWrite64_page_00
race:MTGS::MainLoop
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# TRACKED - one entry left, worker-vs-worker inside a single draw.
#
# The host-transfer-vs-draw races previously listed here
# (WriteImageX -> WritePixel4HH/4HL/8H against DrawRectT/FillBlock)
# were ROOT-CAUSED and FIXED: boost_spsc_queue's empty()/size()
# loaded both cursors relaxed, so GSRasterizerList::IsSynced() ->
# IsEmpty() established no happens-before, and the Sync() gate in
# GSRendererSW::InvalidateVideoMem/InvalidateLocalMem could let a
# transfer proceed against in-flight rasterizer writes.  Making those
# two query helpers acquire removed every one of those reports.
# Their entries are deleted rather than kept 'just in case' - a
# suppression for a fixed bug hides its regression.
#
# What remains is a different pairing: two SW worker threads writing
# the same 4-byte location from within GSRasterizer::Draw itself.
# Scanline ownership should make that impossible, so either the
# slicing has an overlap case or the address is shared state rather
# than framebuffer.  Not yet root-caused; the fix is rasterizer-hot
# either way and must go through the FPS harness on worst-case
# content before shipping (reference: the S2DEX per-draw flush
# regression, 900 -> 68 fps).
race:GSRasterizer::Draw
